From 53e20e090cf5727ee44401f8b812bc22176d3ea7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:49:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui: only the ISO and WB auto keys reset the get_state poll

Why: applyCoreState called updateRefreshTimer() at the end of the
camera-set-values block for every state it applied. QTimer::setInterval
on a running timer restarts it, so any event routed into applyCoreState
pushed the next get_state poll back. A 1 s timelapse sends one
timelapse_progress event per shot, which kept the 1000 ms ISO/WB-auto
poll from ever firing, and the ISO and WB in use froze. Original
Apertar 1.6.0 has no updateRefreshTimer() call in applyCoreState; it
sets the interval on socket state changes and after command and poll
replies (ui-upstream src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp:125-145, :1585).

What: the unconditional call is gone. applyCoreState now calls
updateRefreshTimer() only inside the iso_auto and wb_auto branches,
the two inputs of the interval besides the connection, so a WebUI or
button switch to ISO or WB Auto still speeds the poll up. The reply
and connection paths keep their own calls.

Tested: check_ui.sh lane-ui1 (Qt UI build, QML compiled ahead of time):
PASS, 0 warnings. Nothing can be run on a screen here. On the camera:
ISO Auto, start a 1 s timelapse in Still Mode, change the light: the
green ISO in use follows within 2 s. Also switch ISO Auto on from the
WebUI and watch the touch ISO in use start to move.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp b/src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp
index 6e98bd1..6098a6a 100644
--- a/src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp
+++ b/src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp
@@ -1489,8 +1489,10 @@ void ApertarControlBridge::applyCoreState(const QJsonObject &state)
     }
 
     const bool previousAutoExposure = autoExposureEnabled();
-    if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("iso_auto")))
+    if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("iso_auto"))) {
         m_isoAuto = state.value(QStringLiteral("iso_auto")).toBool(m_isoAuto);
+        updateRefreshTimer();
+    }
 
     if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("shutter_auto")))
         m_shutterAuto = state.value(QStringLiteral("shutter_auto")).toBool(m_shutterAuto);
@@ -1528,8 +1530,10 @@ void ApertarControlBridge::applyCoreState(const QJsonObject &state)
         emit exposureMeteringChanged();
     }
 
-    if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("wb_auto")))
+    if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("wb_auto"))) {
         m_whiteBalanceAuto = state.value(QStringLiteral("wb_auto")).toBool(m_whiteBalanceAuto);
+        updateRefreshTimer();
+    }
 
     if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("wb_available"))) {
         const bool available = state.value(QStringLiteral("wb_available")).toBool();
@@ -1605,7 +1609,6 @@ void ApertarControlBridge::applyCoreState(const QJsonObject &state)
             m_shutterSetByCamera = shutterSet;
             emit cameraSetValuesChanged();
         }
-        updateRefreshTimer();
     }
 
     if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("width")) && state.contains(QStringLiteral("height"))) {
